//  BOTH HANDS, but only ONE leaf may run per tick. Aim position is a single
//  shared resource: when the two hands ran as siblings in a parallel, whichever
//  wrote setAimPosition last silently won, and a buff staff ended up dropping
//  its zone on the combat target. The selector below is the arbitration -- keep
//  any future hand or ability under it.
//
//  Order is intent priority first, hand priority second:
//      healing primary, healing alt, buff primary, buff alt, attack primary, attack alt
//  A hand only gets a turn when every leaf above it fails. On the generated
//  tech staff (harmful primary, healingzone alt) that reads as: heal a hurt
//  ally if there is one, otherwise attack.
//
//  Alt on a two-handed staff is not the alt SLOT. The engine leaves that slot
//  unusable and routes alt fire to the primary item's altAbility, which is what
//  nicemice_resolveAbilityIntent resolves. An ability with no npcIntent patch
//  falls back to "harmful"; that is safe here only because attack-alt sits last
//  in the order and so cannot outrank a real heal or buff.
//
//  Every board key is hand-scoped (primaryTarget / altCastRange / ...) so the
//  two hands cannot read each other's target or cast range.
//
//  CAST CYCLE -- three phases, because every staff ability checks targetValid()
//  exactly once, at discharge:
//      magnitude(focusPos, aimPos) <= maxCastRange
//      and no lineTileCollision(position, focusPos)
//      and no lineTileCollision(focusPos, aimPos)
//  Fail it and discharge drops straight to cooldown; the charge is wasted.
//
//    charge  (wizardryCooldown_<hand>) hold fire, aim clamped into range
//    release (releaseHoldTime)         stop firing so discharge fires while the
//                                      aim is still a valid cast point
//    steer   (steerTime)               aim the REAL target, unclamped
//
//  Phase 3 is the point: controlprojectile:updateProjectiles() pushes
//  activeItem.ownerAimPosition() to every live projectile each tick with no
//  range limit, so an unclamped aim drags the projectile well past the cast
//  range. steerTime must also outlast the projectile's flight: firing again
//  while projectiles are alive makes controlprojectile call killProjectiles().
//  Effect zones (heal/buff) are placed once and do not steer, so for those
//  phase 3 is just spacing between casts.
//
//  AIMING uses nicemice_entityDistance + setAimPosition{offset, position:self},
//  the same shape as nicemice_meleecombat-aim-whip: it reads the real vector on
//  both axes and world.distance is wrap-safe. Range checks use entityInRange's
//  radial "range", not vanilla's xRange plus a hardcoded yRange of 5.
//
//  MOVEMENT is the stock meleecombat-approach module against the stock melee
//  task, so standoff is tuned wherever the melee coordinator config already
//  lives. moveToPosition both closes and retreats.
//
//  The group and task joins MUST run every tick. BGroup:updateGroups() drops
//  any group or task not re-joined during the current update, and without a
//  joined task the coordinator allocates no slot, so every groupResource lookup
//  comes back empty and the approach has no destination.
//
//  Casting is listed before movement because setAimPosition sets
//  self.setFacingDirection, and moveToPosition only takes over facing when that
//  flag is clear -- so an NPC that is aiming walks its slot facing its target.
//
//  castRangeFallback / castRangeMargin: cast range is read off the equipped
//  ability (vanilla staff abilities declare maxCastRange, all of them 25 tiles).
//  The fallback only applies when an ability declares none; the margin covers
//  the gap between the ability's focusPos and our entity position.
//
//  ZONES DO NOT REPEAT. An effectzone is placed once and then stands on its own
//  for its whole timeToLive, and EffectZone:createProjectile() kills the
//  previous zone before spawning a new one -- so recasting destroys the zone it
//  is supposedly renewing. Three things stop the recast loop:
//
//    isValidTarget leads each of the three cast phases, on the buff AND harmful
//    branches. Parallel children are re-run every tick (the same property the
//    group/task joins rely on), so unlike the isValidTarget at the head of the
//    branch -- which a sequence checks once and never revisits -- this one keeps
//    checking, and a fight that ends mid-cast fails the phase parallel instead
//    of playing out its ~5s. Not on the healing branches: healing is deliberately
//    allowed with no live combat target.
//
//    nicemice_markBuffed puts the ally on a cooldown as long as the zone they
//    just got, and nicemice_resolveBuffTarget skips anyone still covered. With
//    two allies the second cast goes to the other one; with one ally there is
//    simply no buff target until the zone runs out. rebuffInterval is only the
//    fallback for an ability whose zone lifetime we cannot read.
//
//    harmfulCastStandoff is nicemice_clampAimPosition's minRange on the harmful
//    branches. The clamp walks the aim inward until the ray is clear, and with a
//    wall in the way the whole distance it will collapse a 25-tile cast to one
//    tile -- dropping a slow/push/forcecage zone on the caster's own feet, where
//    it then stands in it. entityInSight does not catch this: sight is an
//    eye-level check while the clamp's lineTileCollision runs from the feet.
//    With minRange set the clamp fails the branch rather than cast that close,
//    so set it to something past the zone's own radius.
//
//  requireLineOfSight: heal/buff ally scans reject targets we cannot see. Turn
//  off in walled test arenas where allies sit behind pillars.
//
//  debugTargeting / debugMovement: per-candidate and per-slot tracing.
{
